  "body": "## What changed\n\nA stock edit after generation now marks every op that read the stock Stale, so the post refuses them until they're regenerated.\n\n- The stock reaches every generator through `job::collect_job`, which hands its facets and bounds to every op whose source isn't the stock itself. That feeds the clearance top, the rapid-in-stock checks (vertical, footprint), the prior acquittal, the plunge-solid checks, the cross-drill standoff, the axial drill's reach and R plane, and the lathe meridian bar. The set is made explicit and tested as `operation::reads_setup_stock`: every op with a part or selection source.\n- Those stamps carry a stock term: whether a stock exists, its placement, its mesh hash, and its shape kind and size. Offsets land in the placement or the size. Ops sourced from the stock already digested it; that code moved byte-for-byte into the new `operation/stamp_stock.rs`, so those ops don't go Stale. The old Drill-only stock term is replaced by the general one. `stamp.rs` is down from 400 to 356 lines.\n- The term is separate from PR #153's digest of the ops ahead.\n- **One-time effect:** saved projects show every op with a part or selection source as Stale once. Regenerating clears it.\n\n## Pins (`crates/app/tests/stock_stamp.rs`)\n\n- `enlarging_the_stock_over_a_contours_dive_stales_it_and_blocks_the_post`: fails on main\n- `moving_the_stock_stales_the_contour`: fails on main\n- `undoing_the_stock_edit_returns_the_contour_to_ok`, which also checks the post goes through again: fails on main\n- `the_work_material_is_not_a_stock_input`\n\n## Readings\n\nAll app test binaries except the slow center_cut_multiaxis: 965 passed, 7 failed, 17 ignored. The 7 are #159's lathe failures, identical on main and fixed in PR #135. Clippy on app is clean.\n\nChangelog: A stock edit after generation marks every op that read the stock Stale (rapid-in-stock, prior acquittal, drill and lathe checks), so the post refuses until it is regenerated; saved projects show those ops Stale once\n\nFixes #156\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
